module std where

-- lerp — linear interpolation. (Number, Number, Number) → Number.
--
-- Pure expression; mirrors the pre-Phase-5b5 inline JSON-Logic body
-- at engine/src/modules/std.ts:482 (`{"+": [a, {"*": [{"-": [b, a]},
-- t]}]}`).
--
-- The pre-flip body uses operator-form JSON Logic keys (BUILTIN_OP_
-- NATIVES.+ / .* / .-); the post-flip body uses canonical call-form
-- via the function registry (std:add / std:mul / std:sub). Semanti-
-- cally equivalent — operator-form was a pre-`0040` shape; canonical
-- call-form is the post-`0040` shape (migration `0040_operator_form_
-- to_call.sql` rewrote stored data).
--
-- No self-recursion concern: lerp ≠ add/mul/sub. All 3 inner calls
-- dispatch to substrate-leaf specs (std:add / std:mul / std:sub)
-- whose own inline-JSON-Logic bodies stay BLOCKED by the 5b4
-- substrate-leaf-identity finding.

@label "Linear interpolate"
@description "Linear interpolation: lerp a b t = a + (b - a) * t. At t=0 returns a, at t=1 returns b. Not clamped — t outside [0, 1] extrapolates."
@tags "numeric" "interpolation"
lerp : (a: Number) -> (b: Number) -> (t: Number) -> Number
lerp a b t = a + (b - a) * t
